Feature: Update bai_sales.sql to incorporate conditional logic for br_gpo_flag and competitor_flag for biosimilar sales suppression

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And the columns available are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp, integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars, br_gpo_flag, cdl_effective_date
    And biosimilar brands are "Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni"
    And br_gpo_flag may be NULL, empty string, or contain text such as "KAISER"
    And competitor_flag is a boolean and must be cast to string in the output
    And suppression of units/dollars for biosimilar brands occurs only when br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER" (case-insensitive)
    And if br_gpo_flag is NULL, treat it as empty string for all logic
    And output columns must include competitor_flag as string

  Scenario: Happy path - biosimilar brand with br_gpo_flag containing "KAISER"
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "Kanjinti"
    And br_gpo_flag = "KAISER PERMANENTE"
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are suppressed to 0
    And competitor_flag is cast to string in the output

  Scenario: Happy path - biosimilar brand with br_gpo_flag not containing "KAISER"
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "Mvasi"
    And br_gpo_flag = "CARDINAL HEALTH"
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not suppressed
    And competitor_flag is cast to string in the output

  Scenario: Happy path - biosimilar brand with br_gpo_flag as NULL
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "Riabni"
    And br_gpo_flag is NULL
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not suppressed
    And competitor_flag is cast to string in the output

  Scenario: Happy path - non-biosimilar brand with any br_gpo_flag value
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "Herceptin"
    And br_gpo_flag = "KAISER PERMANENTE"
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not suppressed
    And competitor_flag is cast to string in the output

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - invalid competitor_flag value
    Given a row with competitor_flag = <invalid_value>
    When the query is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid competitor_flag value: <invalid_value>"

    Examples:
      | invalid_value |
      | "not_boolean" |
      | 123           |
      | NULL          |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven suppression logic for biosimilar brands
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = <brand>
    And br_gpo_flag = <gpo_flag>
    And integrated_units = <units>
    And integrated_normalized_units = <normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars = <dollars>
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units in output is <expected_units>
    And integrated_normalized_units in output is <expected_normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars in output is <expected_dollars>
    And competitor_flag is cast to string in the output

    Examples:
      | brand     | gpo_flag             | units | normalized_units | dollars | expected_units | expected_normalized_units | expected_dollars |
      | Kanjinti  | "KAISER"             | 100   | 90               | 1000.0  | 0             | 0                        | 0               |
      | Mvasi     | "kaiser permanente"  | 200   | 180              | 2000.0  | 0             | 0                        | 0               |
      | Riabni    | "CARDINAL HEALTH"    | 300   | 270              | 3000.0  | 300           | 270                      | 3000.0          |
      | Kanjinti  | NULL                 | 400   | 360              | 4000.0  | 400           | 360                      | 4000.0          |
      | Mvasi     | ""                   | 500   | 450              | 5000.0  | 500           | 450                      | 5000.0          |
      | Herceptin | "KAISER"             | 600   | 540              | 6000.0  | 600           | 540                      | 6000.0          |

  Scenario: SQL output includes competitor_flag as string
    Given the query is executed
    Then the output column competitor_flag is of type string
    And values are "true" or "false" as string

  Scenario: SQL output includes correct grouping
    Given the query is executed
    Then the GROUP BY clause includes brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, channel_name, transaction_timestamp, competitor_flag

  Scenario: SQL output logic for br_gpo_flag NULL handling
    Given a row with br_gpo_flag = NULL
    When the query is executed
    Then br_gpo_flag is treated as empty string in all logic

  Scenario: SQL output logic for br_gpo_flag case-insensitive matching
    Given a row with br_gpo_flag = "kaiser permanente"
    When the query is executed
    Then suppression logic matches br_gpo_flag case-insensitively

  Scenario: SQL output logic for biosimilar brand name case-insensitive matching
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name = "KANJINTI"
    When the query is executed
    Then suppression logic matches brand_normalized_name case-insensitively

  Scenario: SQL output logic for market filter
    Given the query is executed
    Then only rows where lower(market_normalized_name) in ('trastuzumab-anns','bevacizumab-awwb','rituximab market') are included

  Scenario: SQL output logic for transaction date filter
    Given the query is executed
    Then only rows where substring(transaction_timestamp,1,10) >= add_months(cdl_effective_date, -36) are included

  Scenario: SQL output logic for final SELECT
    Given the query is executed
    Then the output columns are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, channel_name, transaction_timestamp, competitor_flag (as string), sum(integrated_units), sum(integrated_normalized_units), sum(integrated_dollars)

  Scenario: SQL output logic for suppression
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name in ("Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni")
    And br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER" (case-insensitive)
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are set to 0 in the output

  Scenario: SQL output logic for no suppression
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name in ("Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni")
    And br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER" (case-insensitive)
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not suppressed in the output

  Scenario: SQL output logic for non-biosimilar brands
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name not in ("Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni")
    When the query is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are not suppressed in the output

  Scenario: SQL output logic for competitor_flag casting
    Given a row with competitor_flag = true
    When the query is executed
    Then competitor_flag in output is "true"
    Given a row with competitor_flag = false
    When the query is executed
    Then competitor_flag in output is "false"

  Scenario: SQL output logic for error on invalid competitor_flag
    Given a row with competitor_flag not boolean
    When the query is executed
    Then an error is raised with message "Invalid competitor_flag value"

  Scenario: SQL output logic for NULL competitor_flag
    Given a row with competitor_flag = NULL
    When the query is executed
    Then competitor_flag in output is "NULL"

  Scenario: SQL output logic for br_gpo_flag empty string
    Given a row with br_gpo_flag = ""
    When the query is executed
    Then br_gpo_flag is treated as empty string in all logic

  Scenario: SQL output logic for br_gpo_flag with leading/trailing spaces
    Given a row with br_gpo_flag = "  KAISER  "
    When the query is executed
    Then suppression logic matches br_gpo_flag after trimming spaces

  Scenario: SQL output logic for multiple biosimilar brands in one group
    Given multiple rows with brand_normalized_name in ("Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni") and br_gpo_flag containing "KAISER"
    When the query is executed
    Then all integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are suppressed to 0 in the output group

  Scenario: SQL output logic for group by competitor_flag
    Given the query is executed
    Then the GROUP BY clause includes competitor_flag (cast to string)

  Scenario: SQL output logic for NULL handling in all columns
    Given a row with any column as NULL
    When the query is executed
    Then NULL values are handled according to SQL default aggregation rules

  Scenario: SQL output logic for final SQL
    Given the requirements above
    When the query is executed
    Then the final SQL logic is:

      """
      select
        brand_normalized_name,
        normalized_name,
        market_normalized_name,
        channel_name,
        transaction_timestamp,
        cast(competitor_flag as string) as competitor_flag,
        sum(
          case
            when lower(brand_normalized_name) in ('kanjinti','mvasi','riabni')
              and instr(lower(coalesce(br_gpo_flag, '')), 'kaiser') > 0
            then 0
            else integrated_units
          end
        ) as integrated_units,
        sum(
          case
            when lower(brand_normalized_name) in ('kanjinti','mvasi','riabni')
              and instr(lower(coalesce(br_gpo_flag, '')), 'kaiser') > 0
            then 0
            else integrated_normalized_units
          end
        ) as integrated_normalized_units,
        sum(
          case
            when lower(brand_normalized_name) in ('kanjinti','mvasi','riabni')
              and instr(lower(coalesce(br_gpo_flag, '')), 'kaiser') > 0
            then 0
            else integrated_dollars
          end
        ) as integrated_dollars
      from
        purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
      where
        substring(transaction_timestamp,1,10) >= add_months(cdl_effective_date, -36)
        and lower(market_normalized_name) in ('trastuzumab-anns','bevacizumab-awwb','rituximab market')
      group by
        brand_normalized_name,
        normalized_name,
        market_normalized_name,
        channel_name,
        transaction_timestamp,
        cast(competitor_flag as string)
      """
